* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim (issue #27, Part of #16)
* Charge-pump DC characterisation: output current vs. output voltage
* (compliance sweep) at a fixed cascode-mirror reference current (the trim
* code), PVT corner, supply and UP/DN switch state.
*
* `../testbench/run.sh` substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib section:
* mos_tt/mos_ss/mos_ff/mos_sf/mos_fs), @TEMP@ (degC), @VDD@ (supply, V),
* @IREF@ (mirror reference current, A), @UPV@/@DNV@ (the two switch-input
* voltages, each 0 or @VDD@) per ../corners/matrix.md, and @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@
* (resolved filesystem path -- ngspice's `.lib` parser does not expand
* shell/OS environment variables, issue #44).
*
* Includes `cp_snap.spice`, a verbatim copy of the frozen
* ../netlist-snapshots/cp.spice (no edit, no strip -- unlike the
* sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table record, this DUT needs no netlist derivation).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BIAS: FOUR REFERENCE CURRENTS INTO THE BLOCK'S OWN ON-CHIP BIAS REPLICA
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Since issue #72 (spec/decision-records/DR-006), `cp.sch` carries its own
* high-swing cascode bias replica (MBP/MBPC/MCP, MBN/MBNC/MCN), and its
* IBP/ICP/IBN/ICN pins are CURRENT inputs, not voltage inputs. This testbench
* therefore drives each of the four with an ideal @IREF@ reference current and
* holds NO bias device of its own -- the earlier revision's XMREF* replica
* stack (a testbench-local stand-in for the then-absent on-chip diodes, see
* ../records/RECORD-001 "What is real here, and what is testbench") is gone
* because the design now contains the thing it was standing in for.
*
* What is still testbench-local, and still a real design gap: the reference
* CURRENT itself. A bandgap-referenced Iref block does not exist in
* design/sg13cmos5l/, so @IREF@ here is an ideal current source. The trim code
* is @IREF@, exactly as in ../records/RECORD-001, and the measured Icp is the
* block's own copy of it -- so the trim table below stays directly comparable
* to that record's.
*
* Why four sources and not two: the mirror-bias node (IBP/IBN) and the
* cascode-bias node (ICP/ICN) are separate branches of a high-swing cascode
* bias by construction -- tying them together is exactly the defect issue #72
* fixed. All four scale with the trim code, so the mirror ratio is
* code-independent.
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include cp_snap.spice

Vdd VDD 0 dc @VDD@

* --- DUT: the real, unmodified cp subckt ---
* .subckt cp UP DN IBP ICP IBN ICN VOUT VDD VSS
XCP up dn ibp icp ibn icn vout VDD 0 cp

* --- the four trim-code reference currents (P side sinks to 0, N side is
*     sourced from 0 -- ngspice's Iname n+ n- convention) ---
Irefbp ibp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefcp icp 0 dc @IREF@
Irefbn 0 ibn dc @IREF@
Irefcn 0 icn dc @IREF@

Vup up 0 dc @UPV@
Vdn dn 0 dc @DNV@
Vout vout 0 dc 1.65

* Compliance sweep: 0.15 V to (VDD - 0.15 V) in 50 mV steps. `icp` below is
* the current the charge pump DELIVERS INTO the vout node (positive = the
* pump SOURCES current into the filter, negative = it SINKS current out of
* it). ngspice's own sign convention for a voltage source's branch current
* -- positive flowing in at the `+` terminal and out through the source --
* makes that exactly `i(Vout)`, with no flip; verified empirically against
* the UP=1/DN=0 case, which must and does come out positive (see
* ../records/RECORD-001 "Sign convention").
.control
dc Vout 0.15 @VOUTMAX@ 0.05
let icp = i(Vout)
wrdata sweep.dat icp
.endc
.end
